---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---
<PolicyLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How Ballmecca uses cookies and similar technologies, and how to control your privacy choices."
  path="/cookie-policy"
>
  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-muted last-updated">Last updated: July 2, 2026</p>

  <h2>What are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small data files that are placed on your computer or mobile device when you visit a website. Cookies are widely used by website owners to make their websites work more efficiently and to provide reporting information.</p>
  <p>Cookies set by Ballmecca Inc. are called "first-party cookies." Cookies set by third parties are called "third-party cookies." Third-party cookies enable third-party features or functionality such as advertising, interactive content, and analytics.</p>

  <h2>Why Do We Use Cookies?</h2>
  <p>We use cookies and similar technologies in a few categories:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential</strong> — required to operate the website and remember your privacy choice. These are always on and cannot be rejected.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — help us understand how the site is used (Google Analytics). These load only after you accept.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising</strong> — used for advertising measurement and attribution (Meta). Within our app, these are handled by the app's SDKs as described in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How Can I Control Cookies?</h2>
  <p>When you first visit our website we show a consent banner: analytics and advertising cookies load <strong>only if you accept</strong>. You can change your choice at any time using the <strong>"Your Privacy Choices"</strong> link in the website footer. We also honor <strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</strong> browser signals as an opt-out of analytics and advertising cookies.</p>
  <p>You may additionally set or amend your web browser controls to accept or refuse cookies; for more information, visit your browser's help section. Essential cookies cannot be rejected as they are strictly necessary to provide the Services.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
